1
00:00:01,436 --> 00:00:03,436
== sync, corrected by elderman ==
@elder_man

2
00:00:05,566 --> 00:00:06,966
(Leonard:)This is cool.

3
00:00:06,967 --> 00:00:09,037
(Leonard:)When was the last time you
and I built something together?

4
00:00:09,036 --> 00:00:11,736
(Howard:)Scientifically?
A little over a year ago.

5
00:00:11,738 --> 00:00:14,038
(Howard:)LEGOs? Last week in my room.

6
00:00:14,041 --> 00:00:16,571
(Leonard:)If there was a Nobel prize
for Millennium Falcons

7
00:00:16,577 --> 00:00:19,547
(Leonard:)that fall apart when
you pick them up, we'd be set.

8
00:00:19,546 --> 00:00:20,826
Hey, guys!

9
00:00:20,825 --> 00:00:21,345
BOTH: Hey.

10
00:00:21,481 --> 00:00:22,581
(Leonard:)What are you doing here?

11
00:00:22,583 --> 00:00:24,213
(Bernadette:)We heard there were
some sexy scientists

12
00:00:24,218 --> 00:00:26,118
(Bernadette:)working hard all weekend.
Yeah,

13
00:00:26,119 --> 00:00:29,589
(Penny:)so we brought you some lunch and
we are gonna go look for 'em.

14
00:00:29,590 --> 00:00:31,620
(Leonard:)Soup, sandwiches
and emasculation,

15
00:00:31,625 --> 00:00:33,855
(Leonard:)just like my mom
used to make.

16
00:00:33,861 --> 00:00:35,091
(Penny:)So, how's it goin'?

17
00:00:35,095 --> 00:00:36,595
(Leonard:)Good. Slow.

18
00:00:36,597 --> 00:00:38,327
(Howard:)There's a lot of tedious setup,
but once we get through that

19
00:00:38,332 --> 00:00:39,332
(Howard:)it should go quicker.

20
00:00:39,333 --> 00:00:41,063
(Penny:)Is there anything
we can do to help?

21
00:00:41,068 --> 00:00:43,198
(Leonard:)You know what,
this part isn't that technical.

22
00:00:43,203 --> 00:00:44,303
(Leonard:)You actually could.

23
00:00:44,304 --> 00:00:47,604
(Penny:)Wow, really? Called my bluff.
All righty then.

24
00:00:47,608 --> 00:00:49,608
(Bernadette:)Can we really help?

25
00:00:49,610 --> 00:00:51,110
(Howard:)While we finish soldering
these boards, it'd be great

26
00:00:51,111 --> 00:00:53,641
(Howard:)if you guys could wrap these
pipe fittings with Teflon tape.

27
00:00:53,647 --> 00:00:54,647
(Leonard:)I'll show you
how to do one.

28
00:00:54,648 --> 00:00:56,278
Hey, w-wouldn't it be funny

29
00:00:56,283 --> 00:00:57,853
(Penny:)if after all your years
of hard work,

30
00:00:57,851 --> 00:01:04,021
(Penny:)I'm the one who makes
a scientific breakthrough?

